<title>UK: Inchcape pre-exceptional profits up 12 pct.</title>
<headline>Inchcape pre-exceptional profits up 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		4.3 PROFIT	   vs 8.3 LOSS</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.3		    vs 4.0</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 10.5		   vs 10.0</p>
<p> Reported profit	  165.1		  vs 146.8</p>
<p> Pretax		     107.0		  vs 17.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   6,263.2		vs 6,295.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Inchcape Plc reported an underlying pretax profit before exceptional operating expenses and after interest of 165.1 million stg which it said equates to earnings per share of 17.2 pence compared to 14 pence in 1995.</p>
<p>Analysts had forecast a figure of between 160 and 166.5 million stg and a dividend of 10.5 pence.</p>
<p>Full company name - Inchcape Plc</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
